    <h1>Inbox — AI-Integrated Workflow &amp; Intelligence Hub</h1>
    <p class="article-intro">
      An AI-integrated omnichannel communication and operational automation platform that translates high-velocity customer interactions, fraud verification signals, and order events into reliable, observable, and fully automated outcomes.
    </p>
    <div class="article-meta">
      <span>Event-driven design</span>
      <span>Omnichannel inbox</span>
      <span>Reliability</span>
      <span>Workflow automation</span>
      <span>Fraud prevention</span>
    </div>

    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>
      Merchants receive customer queries, order notifications, and operational alerts across multiple channels simultaneously. Without a centralised system, messages are missed, orders go unacknowledged, and fraud slips through. Notifying someone is only the beginning — the system must also know whether the event was delivered, acted on, retried, or escalated.
    </p>

    <h2>Conceptual flow</h2>
    <div class="case-diagram"><ProjectDiagram kind="automation" /></div>

    <h2>Core capabilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Unified omnichannel inbox.</strong> Centralises customer messages, comments, and queries from multiple social and web channels into a single merchant dashboard — no channel goes unwatched.</li>
      <li><strong>Order‑linked conversations.</strong> Every customer thread is attached to its related order, so support and fulfilment context are always visible in one place.</li>
      <li><strong>Fraud risk assessment.</strong> Built‑in checks analyse customer history, delivery success rates, and behavioural signals before shipment — especially important for Cash‑on‑Delivery orders.</li>
      <li><strong>Automated order capture.</strong> Incoming orders from social and web channels are captured automatically, preventing missed sales during high‑volume periods.</li>
      <li><strong>Courier workflow automation.</strong> Parcel hand‑off to logistics partners is automated, eliminating duplicate data entry and ensuring dispatch happens on time.</li>
      <li><strong>Acknowledgment state tracking.</strong> An alert being sent is not an alert being handled. The system tracks delivery, acknowledgment, and escalation state explicitly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Architecture decisions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Durable events.</strong> Important business changes carry persistent identifiers and predictable delivery behaviour so nothing is silently lost.</li>
      <li><strong>Idempotency.</strong> Duplicate event deliveries cannot create duplicate business actions — retries are safe by design.</li>
      <li><strong>Acknowledgment state.</strong> The system distinguishes between "sent", "delivered", "read", and "acted on" — each is a distinct, observable state.</li>
      <li><strong>Retries and escalation.</strong> Bounded retry attempts, exponential backoff, and a clear escalation path prevent silent failures.</li>
      <li><strong>Visibility.</strong> Missed events, queue depth, retry rates, and time‑to‑acknowledgment are all measured and surfaced in operational dashboards.</li>
    </ul>

